Day 45: Behold the Cross | Good Friday (Celebration of the Lord’s Passion)

📌 YouTube Description
Today we stand at the foot of the cross —
the place where love goes to the very end.

Welcome to Day 45 of our Holy Week journey.
This is Good Friday, the solemn day when Jesus embraces the cross not as a victim but as a Savior — freely, willingly, completely. He carries the weight of sin, sorrow, and every human wound, and His final words, “It is finished,” are not defeat but victory. A love completed. A mission fulfilled.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you to behold the cross not with guilt, but with gratitude — to see in it the most courageous, self‑giving love the world has ever known. Jesus meets you in your own struggles and wounds, not to condemn, but to carry them with you.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Good Friday reveals love in its most costly and courageous form

How Jesus carries the weight of the world freely and with love

Why the cross is the doorway to resurrection, not the end of hope

A prayer to let the mystery of the cross transform your heart

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, I behold Your love.”

